React -->

1 virtual DOM
 : lightweight js object
 : every render react will react vdom 
 : using diffing algorithm latest state updated  will update in real dom.
 : diffing means compared between previous vdom and current render vdom then we get the changes so those changed will update real dom.
2 Reconciliation
 : this is a overall algorithm which includes diffing.
 : with helps of KEYs the diffing will know the differneces and then compare  differences element trees old and new vdoms .
 : then it commits the changes automatically into real dom.
 
3. React Fiber
 : which is the  re-implementation of reconciliation algorithm in react 16.
 : it can split the rendering work into chunks.
 : it will prioritize the operation like animations ui first and api fetch next.
 : the process will puase and resume again later.
4.React Render process
 : Trigger -> using hooks state updated will trigger the new update .
 : Render phase -> react call the component functions and it will build new virtual dom next get thew diffing changes .
 : Commit Phase -> it will commit the new changes in to Real DOM.
5. Props
 :Props are read-only data passed from a parent component to a child component.
6.Controlled & Uncontrolled components
 : controlled component form element keep the value by the react state 
 : but uncontrolled keep the form value browser dom state instead of react state using ref current value.
7. UseState()
 : it is a react hook used for only maintain the state for functional component.
 : it has current state value and setter function .
 : when the state changes then react will start the render.
8. UseEffect()
 : this react hook perform the side effect for the functional components . 
 : it run before react render and commits has been finished into dom .
 : it optionally retuns cleanup  function for clean the resources before the next effect run or before the component unmounts.
 : dependency array is for component render trigger only specified states if available.
9. Why useEffect Runs Twice
In React 18 Strict Mode (development only), React intentionally mounts, unmounts, and mounts a component again to detect bugs caused by missing cleanup.
10. UseRef()
 : this hook will create a mutable object with current property .
 : whenever this sytate will chnaged it does't trigger the re-render
11. UseMemo()
 : this react hook a memorized )( cashed ) an expensive calculation.
 : it re-calculate the result when one of its dependencies are changed.
 : improving performance by avoiding unnecessary recalculation.
12.UseCallback()
 : this hook memorize a function and it will return same function reference until one of its dependencies are changed.
 : using this to avoid the new fucntion creation when the render phase .and improving the performance.
13.React.memo (HOC)
: this will check the child props are changed or not if props have't changed it will skip re-render.
: if used usecallback hook then if this will get new props even callback still return the same function until the dependencies are changed.
14. Context API
 :context api is a built in feature in react.
 : which helps to share data across multiple component without prop drilling.
 : it has three parts which are - createContext()| create  - Provider | Data Share to children - useContext() | consumer
